# Netlify redirects for papyrusresearch.org
# Format: <from>  <to>  <status>
#
# There is deliberately NO catch-all rule here. Unmatched paths must fall
# through to Netlify's automatic 404 handling (404.html) so that genuine
# broken links stay visible instead of being masked by a 200 rewrite.

# /download -> the status page.
#
# Papyrus is not available to download, so a download page would be
# misleading. The status page is the honest destination: it states what is
# working, what is partial, and what is not yet built.
#
# 302 (temporary) is used on purpose. It could not be verified from this
# repository that a /download route ever existed and was permanently
# retired — there is no download page in the history, and search-index
# state is not visible from here. If you confirm the old route existed and
# will never return, change both lines below to 301 so search engines
# consolidate the URLs; leave them at 302 if a real download or repository
# page may exist at that path in future.
/download     /status.html   302
/download/    /status.html   302

# If the retired route was actually /download.html, uncomment this line:
# /download.html  /status.html  302
